        "Choosing strong words. Instead of the weak verb 'went', a character might raced, crept, trudged or skipped. Instead of only saying 'a dog', you might write 'a muddy, excited dog'. Do not pile on adjectives; choose one or two that create the clearest picture.\n\n"
