        _step("4", "Find the jobs in a sentence", "Read the whole sentence before sorting words. A sentence can have more than one noun and more than one adjective, but it needs a verb.\n\nUse the three questions: who or what, what happens, what kind?", "In 'Her cheerful dog ran beside her', dog is a noun, ran is a verb and cheerful is an adjective.", "Find the noun first, then the verb, then its describing words.", ("In 'The bright sail caught the wind', which word is the verb?", ["bright", "sail", "caught"], 2, "Caught tells what the sail did.")),
        _step("5", "Make your verbs precise", "Precise means exact. Strong verbs let the reader see the action. Replace a weak verb only when the new verb matches what really happened.\n\nRead your sentence aloud: does the verb make the action clear?", "Instead of 'Max went through the water', write 'Max splashed through the water.'", "A precise verb creates a clearer picture.", ("Which verb gives the clearest picture?", ["went", "did", "splashed"], 2, "Splashed tells us exactly how Max moved.")),
